    {
      "startSeconds": 389.72,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "function"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 391.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "taking any arguments,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 393,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "and we put infer R in the return"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 395.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.04,
      "text": "position."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 396.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.68,
      "text": "If T is a function,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 398.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "R becomes whatever it returns."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 401.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "This is exactly how the built-in return"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 403.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "type utility works under the hood."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 406.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "You just rebuilt a standard library type"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 409.08,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "in two lines. That's the power infer"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 411.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "gives you. We can flip it around and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 414.04,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "infer the parameters instead."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 416.28,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Put infer P in the argument position,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 419.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "and P captures the entire tuple of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 422.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "parameter types."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 423.64,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "This is the built-in parameters utility."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 426.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Notice P comes back as a tuple,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 429.28,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "string then number,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 431.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.52,
      "text": "which you can then index into or spread."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 434.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Inferring the input side is incredibly"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 437.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "handy when you're wrapping or proxying"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 439.76,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "existing functions. Async code is"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 442,
      "durationSeconds": 5.32,
      "text": "everywhere, and infer shines here, too."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 445.04,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "To get the value inside a promise, we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 447.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "match T against promise of infer you,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 450.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "and pull out you."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 452.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "But what if the value is itself a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 454.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.679,
      "text": "promise of a promise?"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 456.04,
      "durationSeconds": 6.88,
      "text": "We handle nesting by recursing."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 458.919,
      "durationSeconds": 6.481,
      "text": "If you is is a promise, unwrap again."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 462.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "This recursive version is essentially"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 465.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "the built-in awaited type added in"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 467.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "TypeScript 4.5."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 470.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "It keeps peeling layers until it hits a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 472.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "plain value. Infer also works"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 475.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "beautifully with tuples,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 477,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "which unlocks recursive list processing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 480.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "at the type level."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 482.08,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Here, we grab the first element of a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 484.16,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "tuple by matching the head"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 486.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.84,
      "text": "and ignoring the rest with a spread."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 489.2,
      "durationSeconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Then we do the opposite."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 491.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Capture the tail."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 492.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Everything except the first."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 495.36,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "With head and tail,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 497.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "you can recursively walk a tuple,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 500.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.96,
      "text": "which is how advanced libraries build"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 502.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "typed routers"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 504.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "and carried functions."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 506.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Indian developers prepping for product"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 508.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "company interviews."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 510.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "This pattern shows up in real code"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 512.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.68,
      "text": "bases. You can use more than one infer"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 515.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "in a single conditional."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 517.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Here, we match a two-element tuple and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 519.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "capture both elements as A and B at"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 522.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.039,
      "text": "once, then swap them."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 525.4,
      "durationSeconds": 3.88,
      "text": "This shows that infer is just pattern"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 527.839,
      "durationSeconds": 3.681,
      "text": "binding."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 529.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.559,
      "text": "You can name as many slots as the shape"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 531.52,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "allows."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 532.839,
      "durationSeconds": 5.481,
      "text": "The compiler fills each named slot with"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 535.12,
      "durationSeconds": 7,
      "text": "the matching part of the input type."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 538.32,
      "durationSeconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Clean, declarative, and no runtime cost"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 542.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "whatsoever. Let's rebuild another"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 544.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "standard utility to cement the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 546.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "distribution concept."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 548.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Non-nullable strips null and undefined"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 551.4,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "out of a type."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 553.08,
      "durationSeconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Because the conditional distributes over"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 555,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "the union,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 556.16,
      "durationSeconds": 7.08,
      "text": "each member is tested individually."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 559.44,
      "durationSeconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Null and undefined fall into the never"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 563.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.88,
      "text": "branch and vanish, while everything else"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 565.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5,
      "text": "survives."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 567.12,
      "durationSeconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Never inside a union simply disappears."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 570.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "That's why this two-line type cleanly"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 573.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.96,
      "text": "removes the nullable parts. Two more"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 576.28,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "built-ins fall right out of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 577.76,
      "durationSeconds": 6.52,
      "text": "distribution, exclude and extract."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 581.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Exclude removes from a union any members"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 584.28,
      "durationSeconds": 2.92,
      "text": "assignable to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 585.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "U."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 587.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Each member that matches U becomes never"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 590.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "and drops out."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 591.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Extract is the mirror image, keeping"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 594.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "only the matching members."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 596.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.8,
      "text": "These power countless real-world types,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 599.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "like filtering event names or narrowing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 602.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "a discriminated union."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 604.76,
      "durationSeconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Once you see distribution, these feel"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 607,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "almost obvious."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 608.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "Let's tie it all together with something"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 611,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "you'd actually ship."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 612.72,
      "durationSeconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Say you have an API client and you want"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 615.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "a helper that, given an endpoint key,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 619,
      "durationSeconds": 2.76,
      "text": "gives you back the unwrapped response"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 620.64,
      "durationSeconds": 3.48,
      "text": "type."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 621.76,
      "durationSeconds": 3.72,
      "text": "No promise wrapper, no manual"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 624.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "annotation."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 625.48,
      "durationSeconds": 6,
      "text": "We combine infer to extract the function"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 628.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.84,
      "text": "return type style logic and awaited to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 631.48,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "peel the promise."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 633.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "The result is a fully typed lookup that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 635.64,
      "durationSeconds": 3.72,
      "text": "updates automatically when your API"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 638,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "changes."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 639.36,
      "durationSeconds": 5.8,
      "text": "This is the kind of inference that makes"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 641.36,
      "durationSeconds": 6.04,
      "text": "tRPC and modern SDKs feel like magic."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 645.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Infer even works with template literal"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 647.4,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "types, which is wildly powerful for"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 649.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "parsing strings at the type level."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 652.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Here, we extract the parameter name from"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 655.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "a route string, like {slash} users"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 658,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "{slash} {colon} ID."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 660.12,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "We match the prefix, then infer the part"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 663.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "after the colon."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 665.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Combine this with recursion and you can"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 667.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.88,
      "text": "type check entire route patterns."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 670.56,
      "durationSeconds": 6.32,
      "text": "This is exactly how modern frameworks"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 673.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.88,
      "text": "validate URL params without you writing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 676.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "a single runtime check. Type-level code"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 679.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "deserves tests, too."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 681.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Let's run the TypeScript compiler in no"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 684.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "emit mode to make sure all our"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 686.2,
      "durationSeconds": 5.92,
      "text": "conditional types resolve as expected."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 689.04,
      "durationSeconds": 5.52,
      "text": "We use a tiny expect helper that errors"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 692.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.72,
      "text": "at compile time if two types don't"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 694.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.84,
      "text": "match."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 695.84,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Run TSC and a clean exit means every"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 699.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "assertion passed."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 701.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "No green test runner needed."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 703.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "The compiler itself is your test suite."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 706.08,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "A word of caution."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 707.96,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Conditional types are powerful, but"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 710.24,
      "durationSeconds": 6.24,
      "text": "they're also where TypeScript gets slow"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 713.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.84,
      "text": "and error messages get cryptic."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 716.48,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "If a simple function overload or a plain"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 719.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.36,
      "text": "union does the job,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 720.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "prefer that."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 722.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Deeply recursive conditional types can"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 724.84,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "blow up compile times and even hit the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 727.04,
      "durationSeconds": 3.52,
      "text": "recursion limit."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 728.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Reach for conditional types when the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 730.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "type genuinely depends on another type,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 733.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "not just to look clever."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 735.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Readability beats wizardry in a shared"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 738.2,
      "durationSeconds": 3.32,
      "text": "code base. Let's lock in the mental"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 740.4,
      "durationSeconds": 3.56,
      "text": "model."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 741.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "A conditional type is an if statement"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 743.96,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "for types."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 745.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "T extends U,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 747.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "then this, else that."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 750.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Distribution means it automatically"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 752.68,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "loops over each member of a union."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 755.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.44,
      "text": "And infer is pattern matching that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 758.44,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "captures a piece of a type into a named"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 761.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "variable you can reuse."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 763.6,
      "durationSeconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Three ideas,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 765.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "endless combinations."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 766.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Almost every advanced TypeScript utility"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 770,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "you'll ever read is built from exactly"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 772.76,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "these primitives. Before you go, here's"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 775.48,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "a challenge to make this stick."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 777.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Try recreating the built-in flatten"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 780,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "type."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 781.48,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Given a nested array, produce the deeply"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 784.24,
      "durationSeconds": 3.56,
      "text": "flattened element type using recursive"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 786.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "infer."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 787.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "The skeleton is on screen."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 790,
      "durationSeconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Pause, attempt it, and check your answer"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 793.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "against the comment. If you can write"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 795.4,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "this without help, you genuinely"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 797.36,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "understand conditional types and infer."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 800.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "Drop your solution in the comments and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 802.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "we'll review the best ones. So, here are"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 804.68,
      "durationSeconds": 5.52,
      "text": "the three things you now own."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 806.96,
      "durationSeconds": 6.52,
      "text": "One, conditional types are if statements"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 810.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.6,
      "text": "for the type system using extends,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 813.48,
      "durationSeconds": 2.8,
      "text": "question mark,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 814.8,
      "durationSeconds": 2.52,
      "text": "colon."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 816.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Two,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 817.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "distribution automatically applies your"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 819.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "condition to every member of a union."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 822.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.08,
      "text": "And the bracket trick or never edge case"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 825.16,
      "durationSeconds": 3.8,
      "text": "can trip you if you forget it."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 827.88,
      "durationSeconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Three,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 828.96,
